\description{
\ifelse{html}{\href{https://lifecycle.r-lib.org/articles/stages.html#experimental}{\figure{lifecycle-experimental.svg}{options: alt='[Experimental]'}}}{\strong{[Experimental]}}

A SharePoint list definition describes a list and its columns using
Microsoft Graph list and columnDefinition property names. Definitions can
be stored as YAML files, used to create a list with
\code{create_sp_list(definition = )}, and compared or synced with an existing
list using \code{\link[=compare_sp_list]{compare_sp_list()}} and \code{\link[=sync_sp_list]{sync_sp_list()}}.
\itemize{
\item \code{\link[=read_sp_list_yaml]{read_sp_list_yaml()}} reads and validates a YAML file.
\item \code{\link[=write_sp_list_yaml]{write_sp_list_yaml()}} writes a definition or an existing list to a YAML
file.
\item \code{\link[=get_sp_list_definition]{get_sp_list_definition()}} creates a definition from an existing list.
\item \code{\link[=as_sp_list_definition]{as_sp_list_definition()}} validates a list with the same structure as a
YAML file.
}
}
\details{
YAML format

\if{html}{\out{<div class="sourceCode yaml">}}\preformatted{# Comments before the first key are kept by write_sp_list_yaml()
format_version: 1
displayName: Capital Project
description: Capital projects and their status.
list:
  template: genericList
# Read-only properties of an existing list (optional)
id: 5a8b3c4d-0000-0000-0000-000000000000
webUrl: https://example.sharepoint.com/sites/Planning/Lists/CapitalProject
parentReference:
  siteId: example.sharepoint.com,1111,2222
custom:
  owner: Planning
columns:
  - name: Title
    displayName: Project Name
    required: true
    text: \{\}
  - name: ProjectID
    displayName: Project ID
    description: Project reference ID
    required: true
    text: \{\}
  - name: Notes
    displayName: Project Notes
    text:
      allowMultipleLines: true
    custom:
      form_order: 2
  - name: Status
    choice:
      choices:
        - Active
        - Closed
      displayAs: radioButtons
}\if{html}{\out{</div>}}

Top-level keys use the Graph
\href{https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/graph/api/resources/list?view=graph-rest-1.0}{list}
property names:
\itemize{
\item \code{displayName} (required): the list display name. SharePoint sets the
read-only list \code{name} (used in the list URL) from the display name when a
list is created. Changing the display name later doesn't change the URL.
\item \code{columns} (required): a sequence of column definitions.
\item \code{description} (optional): the list description.
\item \code{list} (optional): list settings using the
\href{https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/graph/api/resources/listinfo?view=graph-rest-1.0}{listInfo}
property names \code{template} (e.g. \code{genericList}, the default, or
\code{documentLibrary}), \code{hidden}, and \code{contentTypesEnabled}. The template
can't be changed after a list is created.
\item \code{format_version} (optional): the format version. Only \code{1} is supported.
\item \code{custom} (optional): a mapping that isn't validated (see below).
}

Read-only list properties can also be included as a reference to an
existing list: \code{id}, \code{name}, \code{webUrl}, \code{createdDateTime}, \code{createdBy},
\code{lastModifiedDateTime}, \code{lastModifiedBy}, \code{eTag}, \code{parentReference},
\code{sharepointIds}, and \code{system}. These properties are never sent to
SharePoint. \code{\link[=compare_sp_list]{compare_sp_list()}} and \code{\link[=sync_sp_list]{sync_sp_list()}} use
\code{id} and \code{parentReference.siteId} to get the list if \code{sp_list} isn't
supplied, and error if a supplied list has a different \code{id}.
\code{\link[=create_sp_list]{create_sp_list()}} ignores them.

Columns can also include an \code{id} as a reference to an existing column.
Columns are always matched by \code{name}.

Column keys use the Graph
\href{https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/graph/api/resources/columndefinition?view=graph-rest-1.0}{columnDefinition}
property names:
\itemize{
\item \code{name} (required): the internal column name. The name can't be changed
after a column is created and should avoid names that look like
spreadsheet cell references (e.g. \code{V4}).
\item \code{displayName}, \code{description}, \code{required}, \code{enforceUniqueValues},
\code{hidden}, \code{indexed}, \code{readOnly}, \code{defaultValue} (with \code{value} or
\code{formula}), and \code{validation} (see \code{\link[=column_validation]{column_validation()}}).
\item Exactly one column type key holding the properties for that type. Use an
empty mapping (\code{{}}) for a type with no properties.
}

A \code{Title} column updates the default title column of a \code{genericList} list
instead of adding a new column.

Column type keys and properties:\tabular{ll}{
   Type key \tab Properties \cr
   \code{text} \tab \code{allowMultipleLines}, \code{appendChangesToExistingText}, \code{linesForEditing}, \code{maxLength}, \code{textType} \cr
   \code{choice} \tab \code{allowTextEntry}, \code{choices}, \code{displayAs} \cr
   \code{number} \tab \code{decimalPlaces}, \code{displayAs}, \code{maximum}, \code{minimum} \cr
   \code{dateTime} \tab \code{displayAs}, \code{format} \cr
   \code{currency} \tab \code{locale} \cr
   \code{calculated} \tab \code{formula}, \code{outputType}, \code{format} \cr
   \code{lookup} \tab \code{listId}, \code{columnName}, \code{allowMultipleValues}, \code{allowUnlimitedLength}, \code{primaryLookupColumnId} \cr
   \code{personOrGroup} \tab \code{allowMultipleSelection}, \code{chooseFromType}, \code{displayAs} \cr
   \code{hyperlinkOrPicture} \tab \code{isPicture} \cr
   \code{term} \tab \code{allowMultipleValues}, \code{showFullyQualifiedName} \cr
   \code{boolean}, \code{geolocation}, \code{thumbnail} \tab none \cr
}


Validation rules:
\itemize{
\item Unknown keys are errors, with a hint for common alternatives (e.g.
\code{label} for \code{displayName}). Read-only properties (e.g. \code{id}) are errors.
\item Values must match the type and allowed values in the Graph API
documentation.
\item A \code{calculated} column requires \code{formula} and \code{outputType}. \code{format} is
only allowed when \code{outputType} is \code{dateTime}.
\item A \code{lookup} column requires \code{listId} and \code{columnName}. The \code{listId} is
specific to a site.
\item Column names must be unique. Duplicate display names are a warning since
formulas reference columns by display name.
}

Keys that aren't columnDefinition properties go under \code{custom}, either for
the list or for each column. sharepointr doesn't validate \code{custom} and
doesn't send it to SharePoint, so it can hold metadata used by other
applications (e.g. form order or app-enforced choices).

Properties that aren't included in a column definition aren't compared or
changed by \code{\link[=sync_sp_list]{sync_sp_list()}}. Removing a property from a file
doesn't reset it to the default value.

List views

An optional \code{views} key holds a sequence of list views using the SharePoint
REST API SP.View property names (see \code{\link[=list_sp_list_views]{list_sp_list_views()}}):

\if{html}{\out{<div class="sourceCode yaml">}}\preformatted{views:
  - Title: Active Projects
    DefaultView: true
    ViewFields:
      - LinkTitle
      - ProjectStatus
      - Budget
    ViewQuery: <Where><Eq><FieldRef Name="ProjectStatus"/><Value Type="Choice">Active</Value></Eq></Where>
    RowLimit: 50
    CustomFormatter:
      additionalRowClass: sp-field-severity--good
}\if{html}{\out{</div>}}
\itemize{
\item \code{Title} is required and must be unique. Only one view can set
\code{DefaultView: true}.
\item Other properties are \code{ViewFields} (internal column names), \code{ViewQuery}
(a CAML query), \code{RowLimit}, \code{Paged}, \code{Scope}, \code{Hidden}, \code{MobileView},
\code{MobileDefaultView}, and \code{CustomFormatter} (view formatting as a YAML
mapping or a JSON string). \code{Id} and \code{ServerRelativeUrl} can be included
as a reference to an existing view.
\item A warning is given if a view shows fields that aren't columns in the
definition or built-in fields (e.g. \code{LinkTitle}, \code{ID}, or \code{Modified}).
}

\code{create_sp_list(definition = )} creates views after creating the columns. A
view titled \verb{All Items} updates the default view of a new \code{genericList}
list. \code{\link[=compare_sp_list]{compare_sp_list()}} and \code{\link[=sync_sp_list]{sync_sp_list()}} compare and update views
only if the definition has a \code{views} element. Views are only written by
\code{\link[=write_sp_list_yaml]{write_sp_list_yaml()}} if \code{include_views = TRUE}.
}
